  "terminology_correction": {
    "concept_clarification": "CRITICAL CORRECTION: AUROC and Sensitivity are distinct statistical concepts. AUROC (Area Under the Receiver Operating Characteristic curve) measures rank-order discriminatory capacity across ALL potential operating thresholds in [0, 1]. Sensitivity (True Positive Rate) is an operating-point-specific metric: TP / (TP + FN) at ONE single fixed decision threshold. Previous documentation that conflated an AUROC improvement with a sensitivity gain was inaccurate."
